  "normal-park": { name:"Normal Park, Chattanooga TN", desc:"Normal Park is a family neighborhood in North Chattanooga where the yards get heavy use - kids, dogs, and often both at once. That is precisely the situation where pet waste stops being a chore and starts being a health question, because roundworm and hookworm eggs persist in soil long after the waste itself is gone. Scoopy Doo keeps Normal Park yards clean weekly so the yard stays usable for everyone in the house.", hoods:["Normal Park school area", "Mississippi Avenue", "Colville Street area", "Dallas Road corridor", "Bell Avenue", "Hamilton Avenue vicinity"], faqs:[["Do you serve Normal Park?","Yes. Normal Park is part of our regular North Chattanooga routes and is covered at standard rates."],["Is pet waste actually a health risk for kids?","It can be. Dog waste can carry roundworms, hookworms, giardia, and bacteria such as E. coli, and some of those eggs stay viable in soil for months after the waste is gone. Consistent removal is the practical way to reduce that exposure in a yard children use."],["Do you sanitize your equipment between yards?","Yes. Scooping tools and footwear are sanitized between every property we visit, which keeps us from moving parasites or bacteria from one yard into the next."],["What if the kids leave toys in the yard?","Not a problem. We work around whatever is in the yard and never move or discard personal items. If something needs to stay untouched, mention it when you book."]] },
